.TH PODSHL-REPAIRS.D 5 2026-09-19 "podshl-repairs 0.1.8" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
podshl-repairs.d \- what a package or plugin declares about the way it changes a machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /usr/share/podshl/repairs.d/*.json
.br
.I ~/.local/share/podshl/repairs.d/*.json
.br
.I ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/*/repairs.d/*.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
The maintainer knows why, and the person does not.
A package or plugin that deliberately leaves the ordinary path \(em installed
from a PKGBUILD because it cannot be in the AUR, a patched copy standing in for
a broken upstream release, a file outside itself it has to change \(em carries a
reason nobody on the machine will ever write down.
So it says it, once, in a small file it installs, and
.BR podshl\-repairs (1)
keeps it as a record like any other and looks at it again after every update.
.PP
A
.B package
installs its declaration into
.IR /usr/share/podshl/repairs.d/ .
An installer that puts something into the home directory uses
.IR ~/.local/share/podshl/repairs.d/ .
An
.B Omarchy plugin
ships one inside itself, in
.IR repairs.d/ ;
Omarchy installs plugins into
.IR ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/<name>/ .
.PP
Nothing needs
.B podshl\-repairs
to be installed: a declaration is a file that is read if something reads it.
.SH FORMAT
One JSON object with a list of entries:
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "records": [
    {
      "id": "outside\-the\-aur",
      "kind": "package",
      "package": "podshl\-bin",
      "reason": "Installed from a PKGBUILD, not the AUR: AUR registration
                 is closed. The name is not registered there.",
      "until": { "issue": "https://github.com/owner/repo/issues/1" }
    }
  ]
}
.RE
.fi
.TP
.B id
The entry's identity, across versions of the package: letters, digits,
.BR \- ,
.B _
and
.BR . ,
at most 64 characters.
Keep it the same from one version to the next, or the record starts again.
.TP
.B kind
.B file
(a file edited in place;
.B path
names it),
.B package
(a package built, installed or held outside the usual channel;
.B package
names it), or
.B overlay
(a copy standing in front of a component;
.B path
names the copy,
.B original
and/or
.B original_package
what it overrides).
.TP
.B reason
Why, in the words a person will read a year from now.
Required: a declaration that does not say why is refused.
At most 2000 characters.
.TP
.B until
What would make the entry unnecessary:
.B issue
(the upstream issue or pull request, an https URL) and/or
.B fixed_in
(the first version that carries the fix).
Once the installed version reaches
.BR fixed_in ,
the record says the change may no longer be needed.
The issue is shown; GitHub is asked about it only if the person chooses to
watch it.
.SH WITHDRAWING AN ENTRY
When a later version no longer needs an entry, the maintainer withdraws it,
with the reason and whatever the person should now clean up:
.PP
.nf
.RS
{ "records": [
  { "id": "outside\-the\-aur",
    "retired": "Now in the AUR; the [podshl] repository in
                /etc/pacman.conf can go." }
] }
.RE
.fi
.PP
The record says so once, with that reason, and is quiet after the person has
looked at it.
An entry that simply disappears from the file while the package is still
installed is treated as withdrawn without a reason.
When the package or plugin is removed and its declaration file with it, the
record says that the declarer is gone.
.PP
.B Nothing is ever removed from the record, and nothing is done.
A declaration cannot undo a change, cannot change a file, and cannot switch
on a lookup; the worst a malicious one can do is add a line to a list.
.SH WHO DECLARED IT
The record names who declared an entry by asking, not by reading the file:
.BR "pacman \-Qo" " or " "dpkg \-S"
for a file in
.IR /usr/share ,
and the plugin directory for a file in an Omarchy plugin.
A name written into the file is never taken as its author.
.SH ERRORS
An entry that cannot be taken \(em no id, an unknown kind, no reason, a path
that does not exist \(em is left out, and the reason is written to
.IR ~/.local/state/podshl/client.log .
A file that is not readable JSON is left out as a whole, and the records it
made before are not treated as withdrawn.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR podshl\-repairs (1)
.PP
https://github.com/dx111ge/podshl/blob/main/docs/REPAIRS.md
